@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# CRM retained-history collector repair
+
+## Safety and method
+
+This repair changes only GET collection and PII-free reporting. It does not change credentials, provider scopes, campaigns, CRM records, workflows, consent, integration connections, scheduler settings, or guarded commit controls.
+
+`get_marketing_funnel_summary` retains its ISO-8601 timezone-aware input and 92-day/end-exclusive contract. Methodology version 2 adds:
+
+- Contact and opportunity cursor censuses, stable total/unique-ID reconciliation, duplicate detection, and explicit exhaustion receipts. A 100-page safety bound, missing/repeating cursor, changing total, invalid row or unsafe next-page URL cannot certify coverage. Only fixed provider endpoints receive credentials; next-page URLs can supply validated cursor values, never an authenticated destination.
+- Notes on **every retained contact**, not only current website-tagged records. Four workers use observed provider burst headers with a safety margin; unknown headers retain conservative spacing. GET-only rate-limit retries remain bounded; mutations are not replayed.
+- Request-UUID event identity, HTML/plain-text note normalization, original ISO timestamp and legacy `Submitted at: ... UTC` support. Missing identity, timestamp fallback, ambiguous dates and request conflicts are exposed and fail closed. Exact known disposable QA request hashes are excluded; names and generic business tags are not QA classifiers.
+- Private location-bound materialization, exclusive refresh lock and a 600-second TTL checked against collection completion as well as file time. Notes are not cached on contact-updated timestamps. Cache files are 0600 under a 0700 directory. Returned aggregates contain no identities or notes.
+
+The legacy `accepted_website_leads` metric still means window-created, currently website-tagged contacts. `window_created_website_contacts` names that grain explicitly. Accepted requests and unique submitters remain separate metrics. Current stages/scheduled visits are not historical-ever bookings or attendance.
+
+## Collection is not immutable history
+
+`coverage.collection_verified` certifies the retained GET census and parse quality. It does **not** prove no prior records were deleted. `coverage.history_reconciled` stays false until independently retained evidence closes the historical comparison; a successful larger count is not enough. Multi-day historical summaries remain `source_status: blocked` while this is unresolved. A complete one-day retained snapshot may be verified with that historical limitation still explicit.
+
+The reporting workspace now distinguishes auth failures from collector/history gaps and withholds cumulative CRM economics while history is unresolved. Old official snapshots are not rewritten. The repair evidence directory contains a separate validation revision.
+
+## Executed evidence
+
+The original five-page replay yielded zero September-window requests and 17 launch-window requests. A complete retained census found 1,360 contacts across 14 pages and all 66 opportunities, then read all 1,360 note collections: 86 notes, no GET errors. First-page imports demonstrably displaced older website records beyond record 500.
+
+Observed provider headers allowed 100 reads per 10 seconds. The repaired four-worker cold census completed in 177.22 seconds, below Hermes' documented default 300-second MCP timeout; the preceding conservative 0.45-second collector took roughly ten minutes. Later windows reuse one short-lived snapshot. Larger future populations or degraded provider latency may still exceed that budget: fail/partial results must not be promoted to verified.
+
+Actual stdio and native MCP summaries were exercised for Aug 27–Sep 29, Aug 27–Oct 29 and Oct 29 alone (America/Chicago boundaries). Retained counts and unresolved historical evidence are documented outside Git in the private repair directory; no private business rows are committed.
+
+## Verification
+
+Run `.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -q` in this repository. Reporting tests run separately with `python -m unittest discover -q` in the marketing control-plane workspace. Provider calls in unit tests use mocks, including mutation-safety regression tests; live acceptance of this repair uses only GETs.
+
+Primary contracts consulted: HighLevel GET contacts cursor documentation, GET opportunity search `startAfter`/`startAfterId`, GET all contact notes; Hermes MCP timeout reference at https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/reference/mcp-config-reference.
